 victed of elevated aggravated assault \nand other crimes\, we vacated his 
 sentence  and remanded for resentencing  \nbecause the trial  court (Cumbe
 rland County\, Woodman\, J. ) failed to merge \nduplicative counts.  State
  v. Ali \, 2025 ME 30\, ¶¶ 1\,  24\, 334 A.3d 657 .  Ali now \nargues th
 at the court erred on remand because it effectively imposed the same \nsen
 tence without undertaking a new sentencing analysis.   We agree\, and we \
 naccordingly vacate the judgment again.   \nI.  BACKGROUND \n [¶2]  The d
 etails of Ali’s crimes and trial are described in our opinion in \nhis f
 irst appeal.  See id. ¶¶ 3 -10.  As relevant here\, Ali was found guilty
